#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""yog: a review brief for a pull request, written before a human reads it.

Plain code computes the facts: every changed unit of the diff, red flags, test
file pairing, dependency changes and the claims made in the PR text. An AI agent
then groups the change by concern, answers every claim, ranks risk with
citations and lists questions. `check` recomputes the facts from git and refuses
any brief that leaves a change unassigned, ranks a hard-flagged change below
high, or cites lines that are not in the diff.

Works in any git checkout with an authenticated GitHub CLI (gh). No dependencies
beyond python3 (3.8+), git and gh. Not tied to any AI agent. Writes nothing to
GitHub.

The same file ships two ways, and each works without the other:
  - the gh-yog GitHub CLI extension, run as `gh yog`
    https://github.com/ElijahKotyluk/gh-yog (source of truth)
  - bundled with the yog agent skill, run as `scripts/yog`
    https://github.com/ElijahKotyluk/yog

Subcommands:
  collect   fetch a PR (or take local commits), compute the facts, write a brief template
  facts     print the computed facts, no AI involved
  hunks     print units of the diff with line numbers, for reading
  show      print a file at the PR's head (or base) commit with line numbers
  check     recompute the facts and validate a brief
  render    check a brief, then print it for a human

Run with `<subcommand> --help` for details.
"""

